    description: "Optional / experimental alternative-or-complement to the `hypergumbo diff` command (WI-zomuk): commit a CANONICAL survey into the target repo (e.g. `.hypergumbo/survey.json`) and let git do the storage + diffing.\n\nPayoff: git becomes the base-survey cache for free (base = the file at the merge-base; no SHA-keyed cache service), and the survey delta rides along as a NATIVE reviewable diff in the forge's own UI. WI-zomuk's structural diff is then the *polished* renderer; the git line-diff is the cheap storage + rough view.\n\nRequires the `--reproducible` byte-repro MODE (WI-sazap) first — a non-canonical survey produces a giant meaningless git patch every run (WI-pifaj churn).\n\nKnown \"commit a generated artifact\" tradeoffs to design for: a CI drift-check (regenerate + assert equal, or the file goes stale), merge conflicts on the file, repo growth (git delta absorbs most).\n\nBelongs to the (separable) aijo epic, not G8. Demand-gated on aijo. Blocked-by: WI-sazap (the `--reproducible` mode)."  # 29e7
